/T (Modern geospatial operations are plagued by fragmented data ecosystems. Analysts must manually cross-reference satellite data, drone point clouds, and vector maps across incompatible software suites. This "swivel-chair" intelligence gathering results in critical latency, with data processing taking up to 48 hours before actionable insights can be derived. Furthermore, legacy rendering engines fail to handle the petabyte-scale datasets required for city-level digital twins.)
/E (Modern geospatial operations are plagued by fragmented data ecosystems. Analysts must manually cross-reference satellite data, drone point clouds, and vector maps across incompatible software suites. This "swivel-chair" intelligence gathering results in critical latency, with data processing taking up to 48 hours before actionable insights can be derived. Furthermore, legacy rendering engines fail to handle the petabyte-scale datasets required for city-level digital twins.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [27]
>>
